# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-

* Dribble

Implement the dribble feature.

The CLHS doesn't specify CL:DRIBBLE in all details, so here are implementation specific details.

** Activation and deactivation

Dribble may be activated on the command line with the options =--dribble= or =--drible=$file=.

It may be activated by calling the COMMON-LISP function =(dribble &optional pathname)=
with a pathname.

Without a pathname parameter, it closes the current dribble and deactivate dribbling.


| Option                  | Lisp fonction                          | Dribble stored in file:                               |
|-------------------------+----------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------|
| --dribble               | (dribble (bocl:dribble-file-pathname)) | =${XDG_STATE_HOME}/bocl/dribbles/20260626T143218.log= |
|                         |                                        |                                                       |
| --dribble=$dribble_file | (dribble "$dribble-file")              | $dribble_file                                         |
|                         |                                        |                                                       |
|                         | (dribble) if dribble was on            | ; close the previous dribble file                     |
|                         |                                        |                                                       |

The file name is the date of start of the dribble in iso-8601 format
=YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS= with a '.log' file type.

In all cases, if the dribble file already exists it is appended to.

The content of the file is a header line followed by a sequence of
REPL interactions with the following format:

Header format, one lines:

    #+begin_src
    ;; H: bocl $bocl_version
    #+end_src

Interaction block format, repeated:
    #+begin_src
    input
    ;; O: standard output line
    ;; E: error output line
    ;; C: condition/error message
    #+end_src

=input= is the input entered by the user; it's usually a lisp form, but
it can also be a debugger command, or input to the program (line
buffer).

Output can be produced on the standard output stream, or the error
output stream.  Each line is processed independently.  If some output
from the other stream is produced before a new-line on the first
stream is issued, a new-line is deemed separating them.

Each line of output is printed out, prefixed by ";; O: " or ";; E: "
depending on it source (standard-output -> O, or error output -> E).

If an error occurs, The condition / error message is displayed on
lines prefixed by ";; C: ". (This may be redundant with output from a
debugger, but we don't mind).

** Result of the Function DRIBBLE

Then function DRIBBLE returns the absolute path of the
dribble file it just openned, or NIL when it just closed it and
stopped dribbling.

** Function BOCL:DRIBBLE-FILE-PATHNAME (&key (type "log") (time-zone nil))

type---the pathname-type of the returned dribble-file-name.

time-zone---NIL, :utc or a Common-Lisp time-zone.

    time zone n. a rational multiple of 1/3600 between -24 (inclusive)
    and 24 (inclusive) that represents a time zone as a number of
    hours offset from Greenwich Mean Time. Time zone values increase
    with motion to the west, so Massachusetts, U.S.A. is in time zone
    5, California, U.S.A. is time zone 8, and Moscow, Russia is time
    zone -3. (When ``daylight savings time'' is separately represented
    as an argument or return value, the time zone that accompanies it
    does not depend on whether daylight savings time is in effect.)

This function is a helper to generate the pathname of the next dribble file.
It returns an absolute physical pathname.

| time-zone | description         | pathname-name         |
|-----------+---------------------+-----------------------|
| NIL       | local time zone     | YYYYMMDDTHHHMMSS      |
| :UTC      | UTC time zone       | YYYYMMDDTHHHMMSSZ     |
| ratio     | specified time zone | YYYYMMDDTHHHMMSS±HHMM |

Note: :time-zone :utc returns YYYYMMDDTHHHMMSSZ
while :time-zone 0    returns YYYYMMDDTHHHMMSS+0000
they're both the same time with the same digits.

#+begin_example
$ (bocl:dribble-file-pathname)
==> #P"/Users/pjb/.local/state/bocl/dribbles/20260626T143218.log"
#+end_example

** Example

#+begin_src
$ bocl --no-init --quiet

bocl> (+ 1 2 3)

6
bocl> (/ 0)


Debugger invoked on condition of type SIMPLE-ERROR:
  In num_combine: ARITHMETIC ERROR: Division by zero

Backtrace (innermost frame first):
  0: (LAMBDA COMMON-LISP::C)
  1: HANDLER-BIND
  2: restart ABORT
  3: BLOCK COMMON-LISP::DONE
  4: (COMMON-LISP::%REPL-EVAL COMMON-LISP::FORM)
  5: CATCH BOCL::%QUIT-CATCH-TAG

Available restarts:
  0: [ABORT]

debug> 0

NIL
bocl> (dribble)
NIL
bocl> (- 1 2 3)
-4
bocl> (quit)
$
#+end_src

produces a dribble file =trace.sexp=:

#+begin_src
(+ 1 2 3)
;; O: 6
(/ 0)
;; C: ARITHMETIC ERROR: Division by zero
;; O: Debugger invoked on condition of type SIMPLE-ERROR:
;; O:   In num_combine: ARITHMETIC ERROR: Division by zero
;; O:
;; O: Backtrace (innermost frame first):
;; O:   0: (LAMBDA COMMON-LISP::C)
;; O:   1: HANDLER-BIND
;; O:   2: restart ABORT
;; O:   3: BLOCK COMMON-LISP::DONE
;; O:   4: (COMMON-LISP::%REPL-EVAL COMMON-LISP::FORM)
;; O:   5: CATCH BOCL::%QUIT-CATCH-TAG
;; O:
;; O: Available restarts:
;; O:   0: [ABORT]
0
;; O: NIL
(dribble)
#+end_src

